# Gate incidents — appended by run_tests.sh, never hand-edited except to add this header.
#
# A FALLBACK means the sharded path was unavailable and the gate ran single-process instead.
# That is a finding to report, not a slow run somebody sat through. Only infrastructure can
# cause one: the map missing or unparseable, python3 absent, or a shard that never started.
# A failing test never falls back.
#
# A REPACK means a committed shard map was stale — a test file was in no shard — and the gate
# regenerated both maps before running. The map diff belongs in that commit.
#
# **One entry is noise. The same entry four times is a defect nobody filed.** That is what this
# file is for, and why a doc review should read it.
#
